P7 PASS  P3's finding STRENGTHENS on the larger census: the rate still
         spans 0 to 0.474121, the median FALLS to 0.090203 as
         degree grows, and NOT ONE of the covers exceeds the cyclic tower's limit.
         The cyclic tower is the top of the range and the range reaches all the way
         to zero -- the rate is a property of the TOWER, now over twice the evidence.
         STILL A MEASUREMENT, NOT A THEOREM: the range is degree <= 10.

P8       THE MECHANISM P3 WITHDREW -- now PROVED rather than measured
         relator 'aaabABBAb', exponent vector (a,b) = (1,0)
         H_1 = Z^2/<(1,0)> = Z, so the abelianisation is phi(a)=0, phi(b)=1.
         THE GENERATOR a IS NULLHOMOLOGOUS.
         tr(a) = -1.5000000000+0.8660254038j   |tr(a)| = 1.7320508076 < 2,
         but tr(a) is NOT REAL, so a IS LOXODROMIC: True
         translation length of a = 1.087070144996
         SnapPy's length_spectrum systole of m004 = 1.087070144996   agree: True
         shortest nullhomologous loxodromic over words of length <= 7: 1.087070144996 ('bAbaaBB')

         THE ARGUMENT, in two directions, both exact:
           UPPER: a is nullhomologous, so its class is 0 in H_1 = Z and therefore 0
             in Z/n for EVERY n.  It lies in the kernel of pi_1 -> Z -> Z/n, i.e. in
             pi_1(M_n), so it is a CLOSED geodesic of the SAME length in every cyclic
             cover.  Hence systole(M_n) <= 1.0870701450 for all n.
           LOWER: any closed geodesic of M_n projects to a closed geodesic of m004 of
             length ell/d for some integer d >= 1, so its length is at least
             systole(m004) = 1.0870701450.  Hence systole(M_n) >= 1.0870701450.
         THEREFORE systole(M_n) = 1.0870701450 EXACTLY, for every n.
         The injectivity radius does NOT grow, so the cyclic tower does NOT converge
         to the universal cover.  P3's WITHDRAWN MECHANISM IS RESTORED AS A PROOF.
         (And this is why the tower's torsion rate has no reason to match the
         asymptotic constant for exhausting towers -- it is not one.)
P8 PASS  two independent instruments agree to 12 digits, and the
         two-sided argument pins the systole exactly.

P9       THE LITERATURE CAME BACK -- AND IT CORRECTS TWO OF THIS ARC'S OWN CELLS
         The sweep commissioned before xB016 banked returned after banking.  It
         CONFIRMS P2 and P3's conclusions and OVERTURNS P4's derivation and P6's
         recommendation.  All four are recorded.

         (a) P2 CONFIRMED, and more strongly than P2 argued.  The on-shell action of
             complex Chern-Simons IS the complex volume: s_0 = i(Vol + i CS)
             (Dimofte-Gukov-Lenells-Zagier, arXiv:0903.2472 eq. 4.6), and torsion
             enters at ONE LOOP as S_1 = (1/2) log(T(M;E_rho)/2), the Ray-Singer
             torsion (same paper, eqs. 2.1-2.3) -- order hbar^0, while the action is
             order 1/hbar.  Putting a torsion in the exponent as an entropy
             DOUBLE-COUNTS THE SAME EXPANSION AT TWO ORDERS IN hbar.  And a cusp is
             not a horizon: in Gukov's own dictionary (hep-th/0306165 sec 1.2) a cusp
             is the worldline of a MASSLESS point particle, a zero-angle conical
             defect.  No horizon, no Cardy inversion, no route to c.  TWO FURTHER
             KILLS THE CELL DID NOT HAVE: the identification is KNOT-DEPENDENT (the
             trefoil has M(Delta) = 1, giving sigma = 0), and feeding 1/(6 pi) in
             instead gives c = 1/pi = 0.318, deep quantum -- the regime where a
             semiclassical on-shell action is meaningless.  SELF-UNDERMINING BOTH WAYS.

         (b) THE 1/(6 pi) ATTRIBUTION WAS WRONG, AND IT WAS THIS SEAT'S.  P3 called it
             'the asymptotic torsion-growth rate associated with a hyperbolic
             3-manifold'.  IT IS A CONJECTURE, NOT A THEOREM: Bergeron-Venkatesh
             (arXiv:1004.1083) CONJECTURE 1.3.  Their THEOREM 1.4 needs STRONGLY
             ACYCLIC coefficients and a COCOMPACT lattice -- Z-coefficients are not
             strongly acyclic, and a cusped manifold is not cocompact, so it does not
             apply here at all.  With Z-coefficients the only theorem is an UPPER
             BOUND: Le (arXiv:1412.7758, Thm 1) limsup log t_1(Gamma_k)/[Pi:Gamma_k]
             <= vol(X)/(6 pi), for EXHAUSTIVE NESTED towers.  Le's own sec 1.5 notes
             there is not one known example of a hyperbolic 3-manifold with a
             trace-convergent tower where the limit is even POSITIVE.

         (c) AND THE FACTOR OF 8.9 HAS A CLEAN REASON, WHICH IS P8's, IN GROUP TERMS.
             log M(Delta) = 0.9624 is the L^2-torsion OF THE Z-COVER (Luck Thm 1.40;
             Bergeron-Venkatesh Cor. 7.7, which is exactly the fibred case and gives
             log|H_1(V_N)_tors|/N -> log M(P_f) -- PER COVER DEGREE, NOT PER VOLUME).
             vol/(6 pi) is the L^2-torsion OF THE UNIVERSAL COVER (Luck-Schick, GAFA 9
             (1999) 518-567).  TWO DIFFERENT INVARIANTS OF THE SAME MANIFOLD.  Cyclic
             covers approximate the first, exhausting towers the second, and there is
             no reason for the ratio to match.  The hypothesis that fails is exactly
             the one P8 proves fails: for Gamma_n = ker(pi_1 -> Z/n), the intersection
             of the Gamma_n is [pi_1, pi_1], NOT the identity -- the tower is not
             exhaustive.  P8's constant systole is the geometric witness of the same
             fact, found independently and on this bench.
             ALSO CORRECTED: dividing by VOLUME was this seat's own step.  Every
             theorem in this area divides by COVER DEGREE.

         (d) P4's 'k MUST BE EVEN' IS WITHDRAWN -- IT IS UNSUPPORTED.
             Witten (arXiv:1001.2933 eq. 2.2): I = -s Im W + l Re W with s in C and
             l in Z; THE ONLY CONDITION IS l (= k) INTEGRAL.  Gukov (hep-th/0306165
             sec 1.1): 'The other parameter, s, is not quantized', constrained only to
             be real or imaginary by unitarity.  Dimofte (arXiv:1409.0857 sec 2.1):
             'one quantized (k) and the other continuous (sigma)'.  NOTHING COUPLES k
             AND sigma.  And the framing escape hatch does not exist either: for
             COMPLEX Chern-Simons the eta-invariant VANISHES (Gukov eq. 3.36; Witten
             1991), so there is no exp(2 pi i c/24) to cancel anything against.  The
             cusped mod-1/2 ambiguity is resolved in the literature by LIFTING (a
             decoration/spin structure, the invariant living in C/4 pi^2 Z rather than
             C/pi^2 Z -- Zickert arXiv:0710.2049; DGLZ sec 3), NOT by constraining k.
             P4's OWN FLAG WAS RIGHT AND IT WAS THE WHOLE STORY: P4 said the statement
             holds 'in ONE normalisation' and that the record pins none.  The sweep's
             reading is that the inference is an artifact of mixing Meyerhoff-Neumann's
             MANIFOLD-INVARIANT normalisation with Witten's FIELD-THEORY one.  The
             GAP P4 NAMED STANDS -- the record still pins no normalisation -- but the
             CONSTRAINT P4 DERIVED FROM IT DOES NOT.

         (e) THEREFORE P6's RECOMMENDATION IS WITHDRAWN TOO, AND THIS IS THE REAL
             UPGRADE.  P6 named Route 3 as the one to re-open, on the ground that
             pinning the normalisation would turn well-definedness into an equation
             relating the level to the framing anomaly.  THERE IS NO SUCH EQUATION:
             eta = 0 kills the framing term, and Witten's own treatment of the
             complex/cusped case (1001.2933 sec 4.3) keeps l integral and works on a
             COVER where exp(iI) is defined, rather than constraining anything.
             ROUTE 3 IS CLOSED, BY CITATION RATHER THAN BY GUESS.

P9 CORRECTED  ALL THREE ROUTES ARE NOW CLOSED, AND THE THIRD IS CLOSED BY THE
         LITERATURE.  sigma is a FREE CONTINUOUS PARAMETER of complex Chern-Simons --
         that is the theory's own statement, not an accident of the object -- so NO
         invariant of m004 or of its family can ever fix it by this route.  Path A
         does not cross, and the reason is now a citation: Witten eq. (2.2).

